{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["And the people went out and gathered, a day's portion each day — even if they intend to gather much, they will not find in their houses except a day's portion each day, as it is written וימודו בעומר. Each man according to what he eats did he gather." "למען אנסנו — since each and every day their eyes are fixed upon their sustenance from Me, through this they will believe in Me and walk in My Torah. As is explained in the pericah והיה עקב: ויענך וירעיבך."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The lemma quotes only the beginning of the phrase דבר יום ביומו; the parenthetical יום דבר יום ביומו repeats it. The final clause איש לפי אכלו לקטו appears to quote Exodus 16:18 with a slight variant spelling (לקטו for ולקט). The text as transmitted may be partially corrupt or elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:43.906952397Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}